1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,390
Greek Island Holidays, can I help you?

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:07,512
Yes, I hope so. I have a friend who's just come back from Corfu

3
00:00:07,512 --> 00:00:13,000
and she's recommended some apartments in Arilas. She thought they might be on your list.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,120
Arilas, Arilas, let me see. Can you give me the names?

5
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,680
Yes, the first's Rose Garden Apartments

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,110
I'd like to go with another friend in the last week of October.

7
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:31,560
Well, we've got a lovely studio flat available at that time.

8
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,900
I'm sure you'd enjoy the entertainment programme there too

9
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,850
with Greek dancing in the restaurant.

10
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:39,150
And the cost for each of us?

11
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,500
219.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,000
That sounds very reasonable! I'm just jotting down some notes.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Now the second one she mentioned was called Blue Bay.

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:58,330
Blue Bay? Yes, in fact that's very popular and it has some special features.

15
00:00:58,330 --> 00:00:58,810
Really?

16
00:00:58,810 --> 00:01:03,000
The main attraction is the large swimming pool with salt water.

17
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,150
Much healthier, I understand.

18
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:10,341
That's right. And it isn't far from the beach, either -only 300 metres,

19
00:01:10,341 --> 00:01:14,680
and only around half a kilometre to some shops

20
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:17,130
so you don't have to be too energetic.

21
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:19,780
Is it much more expensive than the first one?

22
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:26,760
Let me just check. I think at the time you want to go it's around 260

23
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:30,780
no 275 to be exact.

24
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:36,466
Right, I've got that. Now there are just two more apartments to ask you about.

25
00:01:36,466 --> 00:01:39,120
Um, I can't read my own writing!

26
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:42,000
Something to do with sun... Sunshine, is it?

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,860
I think you meant the Sunshade Apartments. They're on a mountainside.

28
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,540
Any special features?

29
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:54,290
Yes, each room has its own sun terrace and there are shared barbecue facilities.

30
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:55,570
Sounds lovely!

31
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:57,968
Yes, it is rather well-equipped.

32
00:01:57,968 --> 00:02:02,180
It also provides water sports - it has its own beach

33
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:05,160
There are facilities for water-skiing.

34
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:08,260
Any kite-surfing? My friend's quite keen.

35
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:16,000
Not at the hotel but I'm sure you'll find some in Arilas. There's also satellite TV in the apartments.

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,550
And how much is that one?

37
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:21,840
490 with two sharing.

38
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,850
You mean 245 each?

39
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:29,020
I'm afraid not! Each person has to pay that amount

40
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:31,500
and there must be at least two in an apartment.

41
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,095
I don't think that would be within our budget, unfortunately.

42
00:02:35,095 --> 00:02:39,050
And the last one sounds a bit expensive too- the Grand!

43
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:43,001
Actually it's quite reasonable. It's an older style house

44
00:02:43,001 --> 00:02:47,390
with Greek paintings in every room, and a balcony outside.

45
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:49,670
Sounds nice. What are the views like?

46
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:54,755
Well, there are forests all round and they hide a supermarket just down the road,

47
00:02:54,755 --> 00:03:00,180
so that's very useful for all your shopping needs. There's a disco in the area too.

48
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,230
And the price?

49
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:09,350
319 at that time, but if you leave it till November it goes down by 40%.

50
00:03:09,350 --> 00:03:11,180
Too late, I'm afraid.

51
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:16,090
Well, why don't I send you a brochure with full details, Ms...?

52
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:18,520
Nash. But don't worry about that

53
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:21,251
I'm coming to Upminster soon and I'll call and get one.

54
00:03:21,251 --> 00:03:23,680
I just wanted to get an idea first.

55
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:27,660
Well, that's fine. We've got plenty here when you come.

56
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:32,039
If you've got a minute, could I just check a couple of points about insurance?

57
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:36,710
I got one policy through the post but I'd like to see if yours is better.

58
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:39,530
Fine. What would you like to know?

59
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:42,660
Well, the one I've got has benefits and

60
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:45,950
then the maximum amount you can claim. Is that like yours?

61
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:48,940
Yes, that's how most of them are.

62
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,320
Well, the first thing is cancellation

63
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:56,150
If the holiday's cancelled on the policy I've got, you can claim 8,000.

64
00:03:56,150 --> 00:04:03,310
We can improve on that, Ms Nash. For Greek Island holidays, our maximum is 10,000.

65
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:08,240
That's good - of course our holiday won't even cost 1,000 together!

66
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:15,330
It's still sensible to have good cover. Now, if you go to hospital, we allow 600.

67
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:16,310
Yes, mine's similar.

68
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:20,410
And we also allow a relative to your holiday resort.

69
00:04:20,410 --> 00:04:23,880
My policy just says their representative will help you.

70
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:26,580
You can see there's another difference there

71
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,380
And what happens if you don't get on the plane?

72
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:32,530
Nothing, as far as I can see on this form.

73
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:35,960
Don't you have missed departure?

74
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:39,110
No, I'll just jot that down.

75
00:04:39,110 --> 00:04:44,117
We pay up to 1,000 for that, depending on the reason.

76
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:49,124
And we're particularly generous about loss of personal belongings-up to 3,000,

77
00:04:49,124 --> 00:04:52,880
but not more than 500 for a single item.

78
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,910
Then I'd better not take my laptop!

79
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:57,230
Not unless you insure it separately.

80
00:04:57,230 --> 00:05:00,900
OK, thanks very much for your time. You've really been helpful

81
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:03,860
Can I get back to you? Your name is?

82
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:11,800
Ben-Ludlow. That's L-U-D-L-O-W. I'm the Assistant Manager here

83
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:21,850
I'll give you my number. It's 081260543216.

84
00:05:21,850 --> 00:05:30,980
But didn't I phone 081260567294? That's what I've got on the paper.

85
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:34,640
That's the main switchboard. I've given you my direct line.

86
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:37,220
Right, thank you...
